prompt: Load the `notes` skill from ~/.claude/skills/notes/SKILL.md, ~/.kiro/steering/skills/notes/SKILL.md, or ~/.codex/skills/notes/SKILL.md — whichever path exists. The current directory is an Obsidian-shaped notes vault that is a git repo with no remote. Do these two things in order (actually run them, don't just describe): first `add note in ./ for: insight: wadler builds an immutable document tree`, then `close notes in ./`. When done print [notes] applies.
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- setup ---
# A git vault with NO remote: the close commit still happens locally,
# pull/push skip. The scratch workdir is the vault; the inline-path
# form (`in ./`) resolves to it without an env var (setup and the
# agent run in separate shells).
git init -q
git config user.email t@t.t && git config user.name t
mkdir -p inbox reminders insights people conversations topics scratch
# A seed commit so "exactly one new commit" is countable via rev-list.
touch .gitkeep && git add -A && git commit -q -m seed
# A dirty file OUTSIDE the seven skill-owned dirs. `close notes` stages
# by directory scope, so this must stay unstaged — the assert below
# proves the skill uses a scoped `git add`, not `git add -A`.
echo 'not a note' > junk.txt
--- assert ---
set -e
# The insight landed (work phase writes the file)…
ls insights/*.md >/dev/null 2>&1
# …and `close notes` committed the skill-owned paths — nothing under the
# skill dirs is left dirty after close (junk.txt is excluded; it's the
# scope probe below). All seven skill-owned dirs are scoped so the check
# mirrors the skill's documented directory invariant, not just this
# prompt's insights/ touch.
test -z "$(git status --porcelain -- inbox reminders insights people conversations topics scratch)"
# Exactly one commit was added on top of the seed (close squashes into
# one; work-phase verbs never committed on their own).
test "$(git rev-list --count HEAD)" -eq 2
# That commit actually contains the insight file (staged by scope, not
# a stray empty commit).
git show --name-only --pretty=format: HEAD | grep -qE '^insights/.*\.md$'
# Staged BY SCOPE, not `git add -A`: the out-of-scope junk.txt is neither
# in the commit nor staged — it stays an untracked working-tree file.
! git show --name-only --pretty=format: HEAD | grep -qxF junk.txt
git status --porcelain -- junk.txt | grep -q '^??'
